# SEO and launch leftovers

Do **not** start this work during routine homepage visual edits.

**Bring this up** when any of these are true:

- Lauren says the site is almost done, launching, or ready for SEO
- Inner pages are being built (About, Services, Projects, Careers, Contact)
- A form, quote flow, or careers application is added
- Domain, hosting, or indexing is being set up

Until then, homepage-only still applies: keep unfinished menu items as coming soon; do not invent layouts or business facts. Do not run a full SEO/GEO pass on Home alone unless Lauren asks.

**Ask Lauren (or come back to this) when the site is almost done**, not during visual homepage tweaks. Planned later: Contact page + quote form; Services dropdown (hub + Pier Drilling, Belled Pier Drilling, Pool Pier Drilling, Home Foundation Pier Drilling, Concrete Pouring Assistance).

## Do when pages exist

- One unique H1, title, meta description, canonical, and Open Graph set per indexable page (do not reuse homepage metadata)
- Crawlable `<a href>` for every nav and service item, including a Services dropdown
- Indexable pages for: Pier Drilling, Belled Pier Drilling, Pool Pier Drilling, Home Foundation Pier Drilling, Concrete Pouring Assistance — plus a Services hub if that is the IA
- Put those URLs in `public/sitemap.xml`; keep confirmation pages and placeholder Projects on `noindex`
- Hosting must serve `public/404.html` with a real HTTP 404
- Confirm canonical/OG/schema/robots/sitemap domain (`https://bellbottompierdrilling.com/` is assumed — verify)
- Request a Quote CTA + accessible form (labels, `required`, errors not color-only, no confidential data in URLs, prevent double submit). Until then, quote buttons that call should not use an `aria-label` that hides the visible “Request a Quote” text
- Keyboard-test desktop Services dropdown (`aria-expanded`, Escape) and mobile menu
- Homepage a11y leftovers: coming-soon links still in tab order; Services chevron implies a menu it does not have yet

## Still needs client confirmation (do not guess)

- Street address (required before `LocalBusiness` schema; no fake address)
- Email, hours, directions, social URLs
- Whether “General Liability Insured” and the Gladiators Construction quote/stars are approved to keep and/or mark up (do not add review schema unless confirmed)
- Whether Our Work photos are real jobs
- OG image 1200×630 if they want a dedicated social crop

## Before launch checks

Lighthouse/PageSpeed on home + service pages, Google Rich Results Test, no duplicate titles/H1s/canonicals, hero still `loading="eager"` + `fetchpriority="high"`.
